    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Oak Creek was incorporated on December 26, 1907, beginning its life as a coal‑mining town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/oak-creek/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from scrub oak that grew near the original settlement site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/oak-creek/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1915 Oak Creek had grown to more than 2,000 people and 30 businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/oak-creek/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coal mining peaked around 1930, when most trains switched from coal to diesel power.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/oak-creek/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Oak Creek sits at an elevation of 7,428 feet within Routt County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/oak-creek/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town lies on US‑131 about twenty miles south of Steamboat Springs, near Routt National Forest.",
